   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello.<div><br></div><div>I was wondering how I can implement the sort of &quot;Go!&quot; input boxes as are given in twitter&#39;s <a href=\"http://getbootstrap.com/components/#input-groups-buttons\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://getbootstrap.com/components/%23input-groups-buttons&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405939991000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1IwVb__THROwvfDookrm3S\">&quot;Button Addons&quot; documentation</a> for Bootstrap. I tried copy and pasting the html example directly into HTML() in ui.R, but I simply get an input box and a button; as if ui.R were simply: <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">actionButton(&#39;a&#39;, &#39;a&#39;), textInput(&#39;b&#39;, &#39;&#39;)</font>). I am learning more about css and javascript, and I may be missing something relatively simple.</div><div><br></div><div>-Dan</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "AK0xfVB1O8wJ",
   "from": "ZJ",
   "author": "5712068fdf482d27",
   "date": "2013-11-27T05:11:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: bootstrap components - \"Button addons\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>One thing to note is that the documentation you are seeing are for Bootstrap 3. Shiny (as of v0.8) uses Bootstrap 2 (<a href=\"http://getbootstrap.com/2.3.2/base-css.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://getbootstrap.com/2.3.2/base-css.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405939995000&amp;usg=AOvVaw075x5pKesDyVDvKL19v5f0\">http://getbootstrap.com/2.3.2/base-css.html</a>)<br></div><div><br></div><div>The code for Bootstrap 2 is more like this</div><div><br></div><div><ol style=\"padding:0px;margin:0px 0px 0px 33px;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;line-height:20px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><li style=\"line-height:20px;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;div</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">class</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;input-append&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&gt;</span></li><li style=\"line-height:20px;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;input</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">class</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;span2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">id</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;appendedInputButton&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">type</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;text&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&gt;</span></li><li style=\"line-height:20px;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;button</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">class</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;btn&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">type</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;button&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\">Go!</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;/button&gt;</span></li><li style=\"line-height:20px;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;/div&gt;</span></li></ol><div><br></div><div>Shiny actionButtons have a few extra properties so that it will be &quot;pickup&quot; by Shiny and you can type <i>actionButton</i> in the R console to see what they are. It gives</div><div><br></div><div><div><i>function (inputId, label) </i></div><div><i>{</i></div><div><i>    tags$button(id = <b>inputId</b>, type = &quot;button&quot;, class = &quot;btn <b>action-button</b>&quot;, </i></div><div><i>        label)</i></div><div><i>}</i></div></div><div><br></div><div>So I suspect what&#39;s missing is the <i style=\"font-weight:bold\">action-button </i>and <i style=\"font-weight:bold\">inputId</i>! So you can modify the above to read</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><ul><li style=\"line-height:20px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;div</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">class</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;input-append&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&gt;</span></li><li style=\"line-height:20px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;input</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">class</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;span2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">id</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;appendedInputButton&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">type</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;text&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&gt;</span></li><li style=\"line-height:20px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;button</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">class</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;btn <b>action-button</b>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\"> </span><span style=\"color:teal\">type</span><span style=\"color:rgb(147,161,161)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;button&quot; <b>id =&quot;myButton&quot;</b></span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(72,72,76)\">Go!</span><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;/button&gt;</span></li><li style=\"line-height:20px;font-family:Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;padding-left:12px;color:rgb(190,190,197)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(30,52,123)\">&lt;/div&gt;</span></li></ul><div><br></div>Now you should be able to use input$myButton in server.R as per usual. You can update the textbox to be pickup by Shiny using a similar investigative method I have shown. </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>On Wednesday, November 27, 2013 12:25:38 PM UTC+8, Daniel Bowen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello.<div><br></div><div>I was wondering how I can implement the sort of &quot;Go!&quot; input boxes as are given in twitter&#39;s <a href=\"http://getbootstrap.com/components/#input-groups-buttons\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://getbootstrap.com/components/%23input-groups-buttons&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405939995000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37tAJobPQoFETbE_qd3BGh\">&quot;Button Addons&quot; documentation</a> for Bootstrap. I tried copy and pasting the html example directly into HTML() in ui.R, but I simply get an input box and a button; as if ui.R were simply: <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">actionButton(&#39;a&#39;, &#39;a&#39;), textInput(&#39;b&#39;, &#39;&#39;)</font>). I am learning more about css and javascript, and I may be missing something relatively simple.</div><div><br></div><div>-Dan</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
